 62. PW 13 Sufi Md Abul Hasnat, Sub-Divisional Engineer in his examination-in-chief stated that at the direction of the Executive Engineer of PWD he went to Chandpur, Kachua to ascertain the valuation of the property of Setara Bhaban, Sultana Filling Station, Biponi Palash along with A Rab and Md Zakir Hossain, Assistant Engineer on 8-4-2007. At the time of measurement of the Filling Station, the Manager was present. As per the drawing and the persons and from the information of the persons present the valuation of the Biponi Palash was assessed. The assessment report is Exhibit 13 series. From the plinth area of Setara Bhaban, the expense thereof was determined and then he submitted report to Executive Engineer, Chandpur. In cross-examination, he stated that before going to Kachua he did not take SP Chandpur with them. He could not remember the name of the Union where he had gone. He did not ask for any Union Parishad Chairman or Ward Member to accompany them nor he saw any name as &quot;AI Ashek Falak&quot; in the nameplate affixed on the said building. He gave statement to the Investigating Officer on 12-5-2007. He made his statement sitting in the Chamber of Executive Engineer, Shologhar, Chandpur from 11-30 AM to 12-30 PM. He further stated that he went to the Filling Station along with SI and Constable. After seeing drawing of the constructed building the construction expenses was determined and he could not remember whether he stated to the Investigating Officer to that effect. He did not mention the Mouza and Khatian number. He could not say any name of elites of that area. He did not mention the employees of the said building. They did not take any Surveyor. Further he stated that they could not enter into the house nor could they enter into the room. They did not take any measurement. He could not state what materials were fitted in the railing and in the stepping nor could he say as to how many rooms were in the ground floor. On measurement of the plinth area report was submitted. The number of rooms, kitchen, bath-room were not determined. The age of the boundary wall was not ascertained. He admitted that they did not make any hole in the building nor did they inspect the record to determine whether the building belonged to Dr Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir. Therefore the valuation made by them has no weight.&nbsp; 

 86. PW 37, Syed Iqbal Hossain, Deputy Director, Anti-Corruption Commission, Head Office, Dhaka, on getting permission from the Anti-Corruption Commission he investigated into the case and submitted supplementary charge sheet. He got the record from Zibon Krishna Roy and obtained permission from the Court for further investigation and, on completion of further investigation, he submitted charge sheet. He seized the record and alamat and also he discussed the record after having received the Alamat from Zibon Krishna Roy which are Exhibits 24, 15 and 13, 16, 18, 26 and 27 relating to statement, inventory and register. He prepared the seizure list on 15-4-2007 and seizure list is marked as Exhibit 17. Three chatans and acquisition form is Exhibit 21. The rest of witnesses were examined under section 161 of the Code of Criminal Procedure. He received the statement of Grameen Bank, Kadla, Kachua Branch and that has been Exhibited. He recorded statement of witnesses on 16-5-2007 under section 161 of the Code of Criminal Procedure and submitted charge sheet under section 26(2) and 27(1) of the Anti-Corruption Commission Ain, 2004 read with section 15 Gha(5) of the Emergency Power Rules, 2007. He brought the sanction letter which is Exhibit 29. In cross examination, he stated that there were three investigating officers, namely, Zibon Krishna Roy, Sharmin Ferdousi and he himself. He did not read out the Ejahar. He denied that Zibon Krishna was given award for investigation along with 10 others on 28-6-2007. He denied that 72 hours were given to the accused for submitting statement of his property. He admitted that Notice does not contain any condition to state the valuation and the statement. Notice did not contain that the accused if in possession of the property of others, he has to give statement to that effect. He has submitted supplementary charge sheet within 57 days. He saw statement property of the accused on 20-2-2007 but did not see supplementary statement dated 28-4-2007 though the appellant had sent the supplementary property statement through the Deputy Jailor, Kashimpur, Gazipur in favour of the Secretary, Anti-Corruption Commission. There is nothing on record why there was 3 days delay of lodging of FIR. He did not state anything more in the supplementary charge sheet. He had discussion with the task force during further investigation. He received papers from Zibon Krishna before getting the order for investigation. He did not receive the papers from Sharmin Ferdousi. Sharmin Ferdousi handed over the papers to Zibon Krishna and then he received from Zibon Krishna. He denied that for harassment of Md Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir, he made inventory by adducing more papers beyond seizure list. In further investigation he did not examine accused Mohiuddin Khan Alamgir and also his wife Setara. He is not definite about the village Gulbahar on which union it situates. He did not examine any ward member and Union Parishad Chairman of that area. He did not inquire about 4 brothers and 4 sisters of the appellant. Zibon Krishna Roy was not in charge of this case while he handed over the papers to him. He examined the parcha, mutation khatian of Gulbahar wherein he saw the name of the brothers and sisters of the appellant. He did not determine as to the ownership of Himagar, Biponi Palash, Filling Station. He did not examine the year price list or statistical year book while valuation was taken of the Banani house. He did not determine the valuation of Banani house with regard to wages of the workers. He also did not determine about Sultana Foundation and also FDR of 25 lakh of Sultana Foundation, a proposed family trust in the name of the mother of the appellant. He did not go to Gulbahar and Kachua. He also did not determine how much he drew his salary while he was in service. He also did not determine how much he drew in 1974 and submitted his income tax return. He also did not determine the income return of his wife. He denied that he investigated the matter on the basis of supplementary statement.&nbsp;
